Cell["help", "Subsubtitle",
 Background->RGBColor[
  1., 0.85, 0.7],ExpressionUUID->"6bbd54f9-9832-443f-a83a-dac1550f5900"],

Cell["\<\
{RayParameters[Source]={SourceID,SourceDescription,SourceTransformation,\
RaySourceNumber,WaveFrontID}},
{RayParameters[Geometry]={RotationMatrix,TranslationVector,RayStart,RayEnd,\
RayTilt,PhaseTilt,WaveTilt,RayLength,OpticalLength,PhaseShift}},
{RayParameters[Field]={Polarization,Intensity,IntensityScale,WaveLength}},
{RayParameters[Environment]={IntrinsicMedium,OpticalMedium,RefractiveIndex,\
Temperature,Tension}},
{RayParameters[Surface]={SurfaceID,SurfaceCoordinates,OffAxis,SurfaceBoundary,\
SurfaceNormalMatrix}},
{RayParameters[Position]={ComponentNumber,SurfaceNumber,SurfaceID,\
IntersectionNumber,GenerationNumber,ConfinedPosition,ConfinedNumber,\
UnconfinedPosition,UnconfinedPath,LastSegment}},
{RayParameters[Increment]={SurfaceIncrement,ComponentIncrement,\
UnconfinedIncrement,InternalDirectionChange}},
{RayParameters[RenderSystem]={RayLabels,RayLabelPositions,RayLineRGB,\
RayLineStyle,RayLineThickness,RayPointRGB,RayPointSize,RayPointStyle}},
{RayParameters[Rest]={DiffractionMismatch,DiffractionOrderNumber,\
NewAuthorizedOptions}},
{RayParameters[SurfacePlot]={RotationMatrix,TranslationVector,RayStart,RayEnd,\
RayTilt,PhaseTilt,WaveTilt,RayLength,OpticalLength,PhaseShift,Polarization,\
Intensity,IntensityScale,WaveLength,SurfaceID,SurfaceCoordinates,OffAxis,\
SurfaceBoundary,SurfaceNormalMatrix,RayLabels,RayLabelPositions,RayLineRGB,\
RayLineStyle,RayLineThickness,RayPointRGB,RayPointSize,RayPointStyle}},
{RayParameters[Plot]={RotationMatrix,TranslationVector,RayStart,RayEnd,\
RayTilt,PhaseTilt,WaveTilt,RayLength,OpticalLength,PhaseShift,Polarization,\
Intensity,IntensityScale,WaveLength,RayLabels,RayLabelPositions,RayLineRGB,\
RayLineStyle,RayLineThickness,RayPointRGB,RayPointSize,RayPointStyle}},
{RayParameters[ReportedParameters]={Automatic}},
{RayParameters[]={Source,Geometry,Field,Environment,Surface,Position,\
Increment,RenderSystem,Rest,SurfacePlot,Plot,ReportedParameters}},
{RayParameters[\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Scalars\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]]={\
AttenuationIndex,ComponentIncrement,ComponentNumber,Conductivity,DeflectionID,\
DiffractionMismatch,DiffractionOrderNumber,DirectionChange,ForwardDirection,\
GenerationNumber,GratingStrength,Intensity,IntensityScale,\
InternalDirectionChange,IntersectionNumber,IntrinsicMedium,LastSegment,\
MismatchCutOff,PhaseMismatch,OpticalLength,PhaseShift,OpticalMedium,RayLength,\
RayLineThickness,RayNumber,RayPointSize,RaySlot,ReferenceOrder,\
RefractiveIndex,RelativePermeability,RelativePermittivity,SourceID,\
SurfaceIncrement,SurfaceNumber,SurfaceID,Temperature,UnconfinedIncrement,\
WaveFrontID,WaveLength,WaveTiltUpdate}},
{RayParameters[\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Vectors\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]]={\
ConfinedNumber,ConfinedPosition,HoleOffset,OffAxis,PhaseTilt,Polarization,\
RayEnd,RayLabels,RayLineRGB,RayPointRGB,RayStart,RayTilt,SurfaceCoordinates,\
SurfaceTranslationVector,UnconfinedPosition,WaveFrontID,WaveTilt}},
{RayParameters[\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Matrices\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]]={\
HoleBoundary,MaterialRotationMatrix,RayCurve,RayLabelPositions,\
RaySourceNumber,RotationMatrix,SurfaceBoundary,SurfaceNormalMatrix,\
SurfaceRotationMatrix,Tension,UnconfinedPath}},
{RayParameters[\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]VariousRank\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]]={\
NewAuthorizedOptions,RayHistory,RayLineStyle,RayPointStyle,\
SourceTransformation}}\
\>", "Text",
 FontSize->9,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.3686274509803922, 0.7098039215686275, 
   0.9333333333333333],ExpressionUUID->"351c9f41-b43a-4b6d-a988-fa552c5062c4"],

Cell["\<\
OPTICS TO DO:
parabolic focuses exactly one direction; average angle in rich is function of \
theta; change the local parabola continuously to follow that\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.945862080410919*^9, {3.988204547112667*^9, 3.9882045481299763`*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.3686274509803922, 0.7098039215686275, 
   0.9333333333333333],ExpressionUUID->"1263151e-1680-4b95-a8c6-0289c691919b"],

Cell["\<\
Seen this way, you seem to watch a parabolic mirror focusing, reversing the \
ray paths.
So, this tells you how to shape the parabolic mirror, so that the BCO is in \
the focus.... APPROXIMATELY.....
Is the r/2 on-axis the optimal emission point is SOME SENSE?\
\>", "Text",
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.3686274509803922, 0.7098039215686275, 
   0.9333333333333333],ExpressionUUID->"ed606b2c-3f4e-6740-9601-a3ca8803abbd"]
}, Closed]],

